       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **25 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for panic disorder or PTSD, or for patients who are sensitive to side effects.\n\nTell me the dose and indication you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg is intentional, which would be highly unusual, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
