     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no clinical indication that supports it. If the order were verified and given, it could seriously harm the patient. A confirmation without a clinical rationale doesn't change that for me.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a mistake or you're unsure,** I can enter the right dose right away. Sertraline is usually 25\u201350 mg to start and goes up to 200 mg/day at most.\n- **If you have a specific reason for a dose above the maximum,** please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. Also check whether the patient has taken an overdose. If so, this is a toxicology question and not a routine order. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222) or toxicology can advise on that.\n- **If the order is approved after that review,** it should go through your institution's process for above-maximum-dose orders, and not through me.\n\nI'm glad to enter a different dose, or to help with a related order such as monitoring or an alternative agent."
      }
     ],
